      "message": "I think the logic there would be very similar to current listener\u0027s implementation. so we might be better hide complex parts under the manager? It looks like @jaewan@google.com has similar idea about callback interface, WDYT?\n\n```\n                new PortsStateManager.Listener() {\n                    @Override\n                    void onActivePortsUpdated(Set\u003cInteger\u003e oldPorts, Set\u003cInteger\u003e newPorts) {\n                        Set\u003cInteger\u003e union \u003d new HashSet\u003c\u003e(oldPorts);\n                        union.addAll(newPorts);\n                        for (int port : union) {\n                            if (!oldPorts.contains(port)) {\n                                showNotificationFor(port);\n                            } else if (!newPorts.contains(port)) {\n                                discardNotificationFor(port);\n                            }\n                        }\n                    }\n                };\n```",
